From 86be604c65995f3acd57cf3a712bb336a8aad373 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenThesis <openthesis@openthesis.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] sentry/kernel: add shared-memory AFL-style coverage
 bitmap

Implement coverage collection via a shared memory bitmap. The Sentry
creates a memfd, maps it, and records a bit for each unique control
flow edge (PC pair) observed during syscall dispatch. The host reads
the bitmap directly via the memfd file descriptor -- no IPC or
serialization overhead.

The bitmap uses AFL-style edge coverage: each edge is identified by
XOR(current_PC, previous_PC >> 1), mapped to a bit position via
modular hashing. Default size is 64KB (512K bits).

The coverage bitmap is exposed to the OpenThesis control plane via
the control socket's "coverage" command (patch 7), which returns
the /proc/self/fd path and bitmap size.

Integration notes:
  - pkg/sentry/kernel/kernel.go: add CoverageBitmap field, initialize
    it during DST mode startup.
  - pkg/sentry/kernel/task_syscall.go: after each syscall dispatch,
    call CoverageBitmap.RecordEdge(pc) with the syscall handler's PC.
